{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound.thetaSq_nonneg_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound.thetaSq_nonneg_mono","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ThetaRealityBound.lean#L114-L124","doc":"**Monotonicity: the bound is one-sided.** Any `A` above a value that\nalready yields a real `ϑ` also yields a real `ϑ`. So the reality check can\nexclude candidates from below but never from above — it cannot select\namong `3` and `3.7067`, only reject `1.5852`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound.real_iff_criticalA_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound.real_iff_criticalA_le","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ThetaRealityBound.lean#L109-L112","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound.criticalA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound.criticalA","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ThetaRealityBound.lean#L105-L107","doc":"The critical value: `ϑ` is real at a positive-leak anchor exactly when\n`A` is at least `A_c = S/(κ·ln²q₀)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound.thetaSq_nonneg_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound.thetaSq_nonneg_iff","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ThetaRealityBound.lean#L88-L103","doc":"**Reality of `ϑ` at a positive-leak anchor is exactly a lower bound on\n`A`.** For `S, κ, ln q₀ > 0`:  `ϑ² ≥ 0 ↔ S/(κ·ln²q₀) ≤ A`.\n\nThis is the only constraint the T5 channel places on `A` from the two\nanchors — one-sided, and binding only at the `S > 0` anchor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound.diagonal_crossed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound.diagonal_crossed","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ThetaRealityBound.lean#L76-L86","doc":"**The boost/spin diagonal crossing is equivalent to the sign flip of\n`S`, for EVERY positive `A`.** Given one anchor with `S₁ > 0` and one with\n`S₂ < 0`, the crossing `ϑ₁² < ln²q₀ < ϑ₂²` holds unconditionally in `A`.\n\nConsequence (the deflation): the T4 crux probe's \"diagonal crossed ✓\" is\nan identity given the measured sign flip — it is **not** independent\nevidence for `A = 3`, nor for any other value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound.thetaSq_pos_of_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound.thetaSq_pos_of_neg","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ThetaRealityBound.lean#L70-L74","doc":"In particular a negative leak always yields a genuinely real `ϑ`\n(`ϑ² > 0`) once `ln q₀ ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound.lt_thetaSq_of_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound.lt_thetaSq_of_neg","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ThetaRealityBound.lean#L61-L68","doc":"**Spin domination is automatic for a negative leak.** If `S < 0` then\n`ϑ² > ln²q₀` for every positive `A, κ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound.thetaSq_lt_of_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound.thetaSq_lt_of_pos","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ThetaRealityBound.lean#L52-L59","doc":"**Boost domination is automatic for a positive leak.** If `S > 0` then\n`ϑ² < ln²q₀` for every positive `A, κ` — no constraint on `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound.thetaSq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.ThetaRealityBound.thetaSq","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/ThetaRealityBound.lean#L49-L50","doc":"`ϑ²` as read off the T5 channel `S = A·κ·(ln²q₀ − ϑ²)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}